# Client data. This repository is PUBLIC.
#
# Three files in this folder carry the client's paid asset and other people's
# personal contact details. Checked on 2 September 2026:
#
#   Fieldwork-Accra-Delivery-Week2.xlsx   10 cells of live Ghanaian mobile and
#                                         WhatsApp numbers, plus the business
#                                         names they belong to. This is the
#                                         sheet the client bought.
#   exclusion-list.csv                    78 real business names, each tagged
#                                         with whether it was delivered. The
#                                         register that guarantees no repeats,
#                                         and a complete map of the product.
#   Fieldwork-outcome-tracker.xlsx        39 real business names. This one is
#                                         the trap: its shared strings table
#                                         reads like an empty template, and the
#                                         names are in the sheet data. Do not
#                                         clear this by opening it and glancing
#                                         at the first tab.
#
# Publishing any of them would hand away the thing the client paid for and
# disclose personal data covered by the Data Protection Act 2012. That is not
# Quadem's disclosure to make, and it stays true even if the client later
# agrees to be named.
#
# The redacted exhibits in jpg/ ARE published, on /services/fieldwork/. They
# were checked by eye first: names become trade labels, numbers keep their
# shape and lose their digits, handles are withheld, streets are cut back to
# the district.
#
# Anything new that lists businesses goes in here too, before it is written.

Fieldwork-Accra-Delivery-Week2.xlsx
exclusion-list.csv
Fieldwork-outcome-tracker.xlsx

# Working exports. Same content as the three exhibits, in worse shape: some are
# faulty (Fieldwork-drop-log-3.jpg lost every line of body text and kept only
# the headings) and Portfolio-page-full.jpg is a single 7,597 pixel tall strip.
# The published copies live in src/images/fieldwork/ as webp.
jpg/Fieldwork-drop-log-*.jpg
jpg/Fieldwork-sample-*.jpg
jpg/Figures-counted.jpg
jpg/Funnel-49-to-18.jpg
jpg/Portfolio-page-full.jpg

# Prospect research and pitches. Added 3 September 2026, after `git status`
# showed docs/fieldwork/prospects/ as untracked-but-not-ignored, which is the
# one state that looks safe and is not: a single `git add -A` publishes it.
#
#   zoe-premium-dental-check.md   a named, findable Accra business, audited
#   zoe-whatsapp-pitch.md         the pitch written for that same business
#
# Both carry an email address. Neither has agreed to be named, and a public
# repository showing that Quadem researched a specific clinic and drafted an
# approach to them is not Quadem's disclosure to make. It also hands any
# competitor the target list.
#
# This is the "anything new that lists businesses" rule above, applied. The
# folder is ignored wholesale rather than file by file, so the next prospect
# note is covered before it is written rather than after someone notices.
prospects/
